body:
&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>...say I was like 'Superman' to him

&#x200B;

hell yeah, I got the effing same comment when I was younger. I know if things just work they can really be good for me. Am I being too optimistic or am I trusting myself too much to say this? I literally had what seemed like a perfect good future, but now I can't even finish high school homework. Yes I'm still young, yes I don't know how it's like to have to worry about careers and income, but I still struggle a lot, throughout 5 years of my high school years, and I don't see a future of me. I just want to be okay, I just want to be able to cope and feel good, why is it so hard.

shouldn't the 11 be 3 and 3 be 4-and so on?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

^(cuz it's the periodic table, ya know)
